# 23. Day 7 Challenge

## Challenge 1 — Nested if

Predict the output **before running the program**.

```java
int a = 10;
int b = 20;

if(a > 5) {

    if(b > 15) {
        System.out.println("A");
    } else {
        System.out.println("B");
    }

} else {
    System.out.println("C");
}
```

### Think Step-by-Step

```text
a > 5
  ↓
10 > 5 → true
  ↓
Check b > 15
  ↓
20 > 15 → true
  ↓
Print A
```

### Output

```text
A
```

---

# 24. Day 7 Challenge 2 — if-else-if

Predict the output:

```java
int marks = 85;

if(marks >= 90) {
    System.out.println("A");
} else if(marks >= 80) {
    System.out.println("B");
} else if(marks >= 70) {
    System.out.println("C");
} else {
    System.out.println("D");
}
```

### Which condition is checked first?

Java checks from **top to bottom**:

```text
marks >= 90
85 >= 90 → false

marks >= 80
85 >= 80 → true
```

So:

```text
B
```

is printed.

### What happens next?

Java stops checking the remaining conditions.

```text
90 → false
80 → true
70 → NOT CHECKED
else → NOT EXECUTED
```

