# 26. Most Important Interview Points

Remember these:

```text
if
→ Executes when condition is true.

if-else
→ Handles two possible outcomes.

if-else-if
→ Checks conditions from top to bottom.

Nested if
→ if inside another if.

Multiple if
→ Conditions are independent.

switch
→ Useful for fixed choices.

break
→ Terminates switch.

default
→ Executes when no case matches.

=
→ Assignment.

==
→ Comparison.

Java if condition
→ Must produce boolean true/false.
```

